/**
\page animation_target_adapters Animation target adapters

Use these helpers to keep controller state independently of the current pose.
They work without rendering and use floating-point seconds.

\section animation_target_spring Smoothing and recoil

AnimationSpringTarget analytically integrates a damped spring toward a target held
constant for each update. Use applyImpulse() for recoil and update() to settle back
toward a rest point. getState() returns an owned position/velocity sample; see
\ref animation_spring_state for its fields.

\note Apply each sample to a freshly evaluated pose. Adding it repeatedly to the
previous final pose would accumulate an unintended displacement.

\code{.js}
const recoil = new pdg.AnimationSpringTarget(1, 100, 20);
recoil.applyImpulse(-2, 0);
const offset = recoil.update(0, 0, 1 / 60);
// Apply offset.x/y to a freshly sampled pose.
\endcode

\section animation_target_contact Holding and releasing contact

AnimationContactTarget holds a point in owning-layer coordinates. lockWorld()
keeps it fixed; lockPlatform() follows the same point in a moving support's frame.
The application supplies support identity, current transform, contact-window
policy, and reachability. update() releases an invalid contact and can fade its
influence. A released lock never reacquires automatically.

Use animationHasTag() with Sprite::getAnimationPose() to read an authored contact
window. Feed the resulting contact point into Sprite::setAnimationIKTarget() with
animationSpace_World. See \ref animation_contact_state for the returned fields.

\note Use a stable support ID, not a body pointer. Cross-layer points require
explicit conversion. These helpers are application-owned and are not included in
Sprite serialization.

\code{.js}
const contact = new pdg.AnimationContactTarget();
const frame = { x: 10, y: 0, rotation: 0, scaleX: 1, scaleY: 1, alpha: 1 };
contact.lockPlatform(12, 0, 1, frame);
frame.x = 11;
const state = contact.update(1 / 60, true, true, 1, frame);
// state.x is now 13.
\endcode

\see AnimationSpringTarget, AnimationContactTarget, Sprite::addAnimationModifier()
*/
